TERS\nThis helps the learner base claims on sources, places and respectful community knowledge, rather than guessing from a single picture. Keep every claim linked to evidence.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the sources, map features or community examples that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your record with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your evidence? If a detail is uncertain, identify what source you would need next. One deliberate, evidence-based revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Writing only a final label without evidence does not show HSIE thinking. Correct the claim or use of sources, not just the neatness of the poster.","title":"Show the evidence","visual":[{"alt":"Reformer profile.","caption":"Diverse Australians.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Profile</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">outcome + views</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Risk</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">no evidence praise</text></g></svg>"}]},{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect claim as a comparison.","options":["A guess with no evidence","A claim unrelated to the source or place","Use an intentionally incorrect claim as a comparison","An answer copied without understanding"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about reformer with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nHero-worship without evidence skips critical thinking. Here is a more productive model: Example: a reformer campaigns for a fairer law; evidence includes petitions, speeches, outcomes. Stu